Run locally
Requires Python 3.10+.
python -m venv .venv
# Windows:
.venv\\Scripts\\activate
# macOS/Linux:
source .venv/bin/activate

pip install -r requirements.txt
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
Open the interactive API docs at http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs.

Upload a supported file using the docs or curl:
curl -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:8000/transcriptions" \
  -F "file=@sample.wav"
Important implementation note
The transcribe_audio() function is intentionally a stub that returns a demo segment. Connect it to a real transcription engine/provider (for example, faster-whisper or a cloud speech API) before describing this as a working speech-to-text implementation. The included background task is suitable only for a small demo: in-process tasks can be lost on process restart and do not provide durable queue guarantees. The README's production architecture describes the recommended approach.
